#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introducere"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following video, John Watrous steps you through the content in this lesson on single systems. Alternatively, you can open the [YouTube video](https://youtu.be/3-c4xJa7Flk?list=PLOFEBzvs-VvqKKMXX4vbi4EB1uaErFMSO) for this lesson in a separate window. [Download the slides](https://ibm.box.com/public/static/95va6f5vqru3mpsv9p5ivwcyxino4rk7.pdf) for this lesson.\n"
msgstr "În videoclipul următor, John Watrous te ghidează prin conținutul acestei lecții despre sisteme individuale. Alternativ, poți deschide [videoclipul de pe YouTube](https://youtu.be/3-c4xJa7Flk?list=PLOFEBzvs-VvqKKMXX4vbi4EB1uaErFMSO) pentru această lecție într-o fereastră separată. [Descarcă diapozitivele](https://ibm.box.com/public/static/95va6f5vqru3mpsv9p5ivwcyxino4rk7.pdf) pentru această lecție.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"134056207\" title=\"In this video, John Watrous describes classical and quantum state vectors. He introduces some critical notation for quantum states and operators, including unitary matrices for operations on qubit systems.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"134056207\" title=\"In this video, John Watrous describes classical and quantum state vectors. He introduces some critical notation for quantum states and operators, including unitary matrices for operations on qubit systems.\"/>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson introduces the basic framework of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum information is both a concept and a framework for modeling and describing information in quantum systems. While it is based on and motivated by quantum physics, the physical details can largely be abstracted away, leaving a mathematical framework that is applicable to a variety of specific physical systems.\">quantum information</DefinitionTooltip>, including the description of quantum states as vectors with complex number entries, measurements that allow classical information to be extracted from quantum states, and operations on quantum states that are described by unitary matrices.\n"
msgstr "Această lecție introduce cadrul de bază al <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Quantum information is both a concept and a framework for modeling and describing information in quantum systems. While it is based on and motivated by quantum physics, the physical details can largely be abstracted away, leaving a mathematical framework that is applicable to a variety of specific physical systems.\">informației cuantice</DefinitionTooltip>, incluzând descrierea stărilor cuantice ca vectori cu intrări de numere complexe, măsurători care permit extragerea de informații clasice din stările cuantice și operații asupra stărilor cuantice descrise prin matrice unitare.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will restrict our attention in this lesson to the comparatively simple setting in which a *single system* is considered in isolation.\n"
"In the next lesson, we'll expand our view to *multiple systems,* which can interact with one another and be correlated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ne vom limita atenția în această lecție la cadrul comparativ simplu în care un *sistem individual* este considerat în izolare.\n"
"În lecția următoare, ne vom extinde perspectiva la *sisteme multiple*, care pot interacționa unele cu altele și pot fi corelate.\n"
